On an early level of the dungeons, I had the misfortune to be bitten by
a wererat, which was blocking me from progressing beyond the first room
on one level.  And worst of all, I kept transforming into a rat myself,
forcing me to drop every single one of my items, and bringing me down
to 8hp.  During a long and grueling process of going down the stairs,
using #monster to summon a rat friend to fight the wererat and his own
summoned rats, running upstairs when my HP was critical, being unable
to eat anything because I can't pick up any food, having my pet cat get
confused from lack of food and start attacking me, I finally end up
with the wererat and its minions dead, myself back into a human due to
praying, and with a whole army of tame rats to do my bidding.

In times past I would have given up early and let it kill me, but not
this time -- I was able to think clearly and keep a cool head and get
out of the crisis.

Of course, just one level further, I get killed in the Gnomish Mines
regardless, but it was still pretty cool.



